      ":question/worked-solution": "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-3,2)$,$(0,2)$,$(-1,0)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-3,2)}=1(-3)^{2}-3(2)^{2}=-3, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,2)}=1(0)^{2}-3(2)^{2}=-12, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,0)}=1(-1)^{2}-3(0)^{2}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](3f9ea46c49615650d7de7bf415298cbe3df4fb097cd15d86273ff41082b75c4d.png)",
